From 586b6aa9ca260e85cf967b753382c2604ef7ab79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:14:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Skip unparseable lines in the fluentd adapter

Fluentd parsers yield (nil, nil) for lines they cannot parse; the
adapter passed nil to the mapper, which crashed with NoMethodError.
Seen when tailing a file while it is being appended to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013kYwHzrj5ef427USqzf3UF
---
 lib/gl_tail/adapters/fluentd.rb | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/gl_tail/adapters/fluentd.rb b/lib/gl_tail/adapters/fluentd.rb
index 4f8d005..606788f 100644
--- a/lib/gl_tail/adapters/fluentd.rb
+++ b/lib/gl_tail/adapters/fluentd.rb
@@ -16,8 +16,11 @@ module GlTail
         @config_hash = config
       end
 
+      # Fluentd parsers yield (nil, nil) for lines they can't parse (a
+      # malformed entry, or a line caught half-written while tailing). Skip
+      # those, like Adapters::Regex does, instead of handing nil to the mapper.
       def parse(line)
-        plugin.parse(line) { |_time, record| yield record }
+        plugin.parse(line) { |_time, record| yield record if record }
       end
 
       private
